==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bake-Nyanko''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Extra-Life Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
One of the stages where this Cat shines is in [[Unholy Tempest (Insane)]]. A stack of Undead Cats is more reliable than Gardener Cat, since their 20% chance to slow Zombies is better than Gardener's 5% chance to freeze Zombies. Combine this Cat with [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]] and various Cats with [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] and Massive Damage to Zombies to kill everything on that stage. Otherwise, it's [[User Rank]]! This is because its stats aren't good enough for generalist usage. If you plan to use it outside of The Rolling Dead, then treat it as though it were a costly suicidal debuffer.

==='''True Form'''===
Extra-Life Cat gains a 36% HP boost, which is good against peons. However, against more threatening Zombie enemies, this extra HP is barely noticeable most of the time. It also gains the [[:Category:Soulstrike Cats|Soulstrike]] ability, which can possibly help against Zombie corpses. However, even as a somewhat spammable Unit, Extra-Life Cat's low attack stat and Single Attack still keep this new ability from making a huge impact aside from slowing Zombies before they revive, though that can still be decently useful.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & User Rank Dump}}

