==Trivia==
*Undead Cat had different stats and a different description prior to [[Version 5.7 Update|Version 5.7]].
**Its previous stats has longer cooldown time and lower health, as well as the ability to [[Survive|Survive]] and [[Strengthen]] by 100% at 1% health, as opposed to its' [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] abilities.
*Undead Cat was briefly made obtainable in all versions through the first [[June Bride of the Devil (Event Gacha)|June Bride of the Devil]] event gacha, though was later replaced by [[Ancient Egg: N203 (Special Cat)|Clown Cat]] in [[Version 12.4 Update|Version 12.4]]. The original method of unlocking it through accessing [https://ponos.s3.amazonaws.com/information/appli/battlecats/news/girlsmons_charaget.html this URL] still works for the Japanese version, however.
**Despite now being unobtainable outside of BCJP, in all versions Undead Cat is used in one of the Fixed Lineups found in the [[Catclaw Championships]].
*Undead Cat was added to commemorate [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' discontinued series [[GirlsMons]] (ガルズ モンズ Garuzu Monzu).
**The date on the gravestone in Extra-Life Cat's attack animation, January 19th, 2017, is the exact date that the game shut down.
*Bake-Nyanko's name references the [[w:Bakeneko|Bakeneko]], a type of [[w:Yōkai|Yōkai]] believed to be the result of a cat developing supernatural powers as it ages.
*Extra-Life Cat is likely a reference to [[mariowiki:Mario|Mario]], both in name and appearence.

